{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfmdUzN4kyNFoV3uaxh5W","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I don't have the specifics of that decision. My notes from our past conversations say we covered consumer groups as part of the Kafka migration, but not which naming convention you settled on, and I don't want to guess and have you bake the wrong pattern into the migration.\n\nA few ways to pin it down quickly:\n\n- **Check the runbook draft.** If it got decided, it likely landed there or in the pre-migration checklist.\n- **Look at existing configs.** Any `group.id` values already in your consumer configs or Helm values will show the pattern in use.\n- **Ask Tom, Dana, or Priya.** If it came out of a team discussion, one of them may remember.\n\nIf it's still open, here's a common pattern for reference:\n\n```\n<env>.<domain>.<service>.<purpose>\ne.g. prod.orders.fulfillment-svc.order-created-handler\n```\n\nIt works well because:\n- The environment prefix prevents accidental cross-environment offset sharing.\n- The service name makes ownership obvious in Grafana and lag dashboards.\n- The purpose suffix lets one service run several independent consumers on the same topic.\n- Group IDs are hard to rename later, since a new name means new offsets, so it's worth locking in before Monday.\n\nIf you paste what you have in the runbook or configs, I can check it for consistency before the migration starts."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":859,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":859},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"afddb86c-c2af-4796-ad52-23336bb2784b","uuid":"f61e7363-6009-40de-b472-28ce1